# Cellular Automata/Connway’s Game of Life

This lab was not provided with base code, so I hastily striped out my trusty graphics assignment. Due to time constraints the project itself is rather messy, but functional. Cellular automata is the idea of giving each pixel or texel it’s own rules and calculating for each independently. In this case the rules of each cell are simple.

1) A cell can be “Alive” or “Dead”

2) An alive cell with less than 2 alive neighbours dies.

3) An alive cell with more than 3 alive neighbours dies.

4) A dead cell with more than 2 neighbours will come to life.

It is important to note that the change is calculated in one pass then applied in a second, thus the first cell to update does not alter the outcome of the second cell to update.

